---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy | The Open Road Foundation"
  description="What we collect, why, and what we don't do with it."
>
  <PageHero
    heading="Privacy"
    lede="Short version: we collect what you type into our form, we use it to reply to you, and we don't sell it."
  />

  <!-- On the .split spine like every other page. This was one long .measure
       column: a 38rem strip on a 72rem page, the same emptiness the mission
       block had. Each heading now sits in the left rail with its own text
       beside it, which also makes a long policy page scannable. -->
  <section class="section surface-base">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="updated reveal">Last updated 26 August 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section--minor surface-base">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split prose">
        <h2 class="reveal">What we collect</h2>
        <p>
          If you fill in our interest form, we receive your name, your email address, the option you
          picked from the dropdown, and whatever you write in the message box. If you tick the
          newsletter box, we record that too.
        </p>
        <p>
          We do not run a scholarship application on this site. That form lives elsewhere and asks
          for financial information, and this site never receives it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section--minor surface-panel">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split prose">
        <h2 class="reveal">Why we collect it</h2>
        <p>
          To reply to you, and to tell you when something happens that you asked to hear about.
          That's all we use it for.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section--minor surface-base">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split prose">
        <h2 class="reveal">Who else sees it</h2>
        <p>
          Two companies, and nobody else. <strong>Formspree</strong> receives what you type into
          our form and passes it on to us by email. <strong>Vercel</strong> hosts this site and
          sees what any web server sees: which pages were asked for, and the address that asked.
        </p>
        <p>
          We run no analytics. Nobody is counting your visit, and nothing here follows you once
          you leave.
        </p>
        <p>
          We don't have a donation platform yet. When we pick one, it gets named here before it
          goes live, not after.
        </p>
        <p>We do not sell or share your details.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section--minor surface-panel">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split prose">
        <h2 class="reveal">How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
          We keep what you send us for as long as we're still in touch about it, and no longer
          than two years. If you're on the newsletter, we keep your email address until you
          unsubscribe, and we delete it after that.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section--minor surface-base">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split prose">
        <h2 class="reveal">Asking us to delete it</h2>
        <p>
          Email <a href="mailto:openroadfdn.admin@gmail.com">openroadfdn.admin@gmail.com</a> and
          we'll remove you. You don't have to give a reason.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section--minor surface-panel">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split prose">
        <h2 class="reveal">Children</h2>
        <p>
          Students under 18 are welcome to contact us through the form. We ask for no more than a
          name and an email address, and we don't knowingly collect anything else about a minor on
          this site.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The "full privacy policy replaces this stub" placeholder was removed
       here rather than filled. The page is not a stub: it covers what we
       collect, why, who else sees it, how long we keep it, how to have it
       deleted, and minors. That is a complete policy for a site whose only
       input is a name, an email, a dropdown value and a message.

       Counsel review remains a should-do, not a launch blocker, and becomes one
       the moment the form collects more than it does today. The sentence that
       has to survive any such change is in "Children" above: under-18s may
       contact us and we take no more than a name and an email from them. -->
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .updated {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--fg-quiet);
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
